{"name":"Arid Plains","hex":"#b6b4a9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"arid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Very dry.","Describing a very dry climate. Typically defined as less than 25 cm or 10 inches of rainfall annually."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arid"},{"term":"plains","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of plain"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of plain"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plains"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aridity","blocks":[{"text":"Aridity is a condition of geographical regions characterized by low annual precipitation, increased temperatures, and limited water availability. These areas, which make up approximately 43% of total global available land area, tend to fall upon degraded soils, and their health and functioning are key necessities of regulating ecosystems’ atmospheric components."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/1893_Arid_regions_of_the_western_united_states.jpg/330px-1893_Arid_regions_of_the_western_united_states.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aridity","wikidata":"Q1330709"},{"title":"Plain","blocks":[{"text":"In geography, a plain, commonly known as flatland, is a flat expanse of land that generally has few rapid or steep changes in elevation. Natural vegetation in plains can include prairies/grasslands, forests, savanah, tundra, and desert biomes, among others. Plains occur as lowlands along valleys or at the base of mountains, as coastal plains, and as plateaus or uplands. Plains are one of the major landforms on earth, being present on all continents and covering more than one-third of the world's land area. Plains in many areas are important for agriculture. There are various types of plains, and biomes on them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Maniototoevening.jpg/330px-Maniototoevening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plain","wikidata":"Q160091"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Horton_Plains_2021.jpg/500px-Horton_Plains_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Horton_Plains_2021.jpg/1280px-Horton_Plains_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Horton_Plains_2021.jpg/500px-Horton_Plains_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Montane plains as seen in Horton Plains in Sri Lanka","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHorton_Plains_2021.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Marmilla_las_plassas.jpg/500px-Marmilla_las_plassas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Marmilla_las_plassas.jpg/500px-Marmilla_las_plassas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Plain of Campidano, Italy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMarmilla_las_plassas.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/AlluvialPlain.JPG/500px-AlluvialPlain.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/AlluvialPlain.JPG/1280px-AlluvialPlain.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/AlluvialPlain.JPG/500px-AlluvialPlain.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A small, incised alluvial plain from Red Rock Canyon State Park 